{"id": "EUVD-2026-102265", "enisaUuid": "2eb3a5b9-3aa0-3382-97cb-8a7389adfb49", "description": "NetSurf libnsbmp through 0.1.7 contains an out-of-bounds read vulnerability in bmp_decode_rle8() and bmp_decode_rle4() because absolute-run bound checks omit the word-alignment pad byte. Attackers can supply a crafted RLE8 or RLE4 BMP ending on an odd-length absolute run to cause a one-byte heap over-read, crashing applications decoding untrusted images.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:31", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T19:44:28", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/libnsbmp-rle-absolute-pad-and-ico-mask-oob-read", "https://github.com/netsurf-browser/libnsbmp/blob/ea063c9f46acb43e90208da14073332b505ef7e7/src/libnsbmp.c#L942-L982", "https://github.com/netsurf-browser/libnsbmp/blob/ea063c9f46acb43e90208da14073332b505ef7e7/src/libnsbmp.c#L1096-L1147", "https://download.netsurf-browser.org/libs/releases/libnsbmp-0.1.7-src.tar.gz", "https://github.com/netsurf-browser/libnsbmp", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/netsurf-libnsbmp-through-0.1.7-out-of-bounds-read-in-rle8-and-rle4-decoders"], "aliases": ["GHSA-2rgc-q6cr-f7qj", "CVE-2026-111138"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "7c8ae159-0409-32a2-bec2-3df2be20aec9", "product": {"name": "Libnsbmp", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.1.7"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "018457d1-e6c0-3412-8d25-58cba17ba2e2", "vendor": {"name": "netsurf"}}], "isExploited": false}